## Summary
- Use own-key checks when selecting installed plugin and hook-pack update targets from CLI input.
- Preserve npm package matching for prototype-named package names such as constructor.
- Add focused regression coverage for plugin and hook update selection.

## What Problem This Solves
The plugin and hook update selectors used rawId in installs to decide whether CLI input named an installed entry. Because install maps are normal objects, inherited Object prototype keys such as constructor were treated as installed ids even when no own install record existed. That can make plugin update skip npm-package matching for a real tracked package, and can make hook-pack update try to update a non-existent hook id.

## Evidence
Real environment tested: Local OpenClaw checkout on Linux, Node.js v22.22.0, using the real exported resolvePluginUpdateSelection and resolveHookPackUpdateSelection functions.

Before fix on current main, this input used an installed npm plugin package whose resolved name is constructor but whose tracked install id is tracked-constructor. It also checked an empty hook install map with rawId constructor:
~~~js
const pluginInstall = { source: 'npm', spec: 'constructor', resolvedName: 'constructor', installPath: '/tmp/plugin' };
console.log(JSON.stringify({
  plugin: resolvePluginUpdateSelection({ installs: { 'tracked-constructor': pluginInstall }, rawId: 'constructor' }),
  hook: resolveHookPackUpdateSelection({ installs: {}, rawId: 'constructor' }),
}, null, 2));
~~~

Current main misclassified the inherited constructor key as an installed id:
~~~text
{
  "plugin": {
    "pluginIds": [
      "constructor"
    ]
  },
  "hook": {
    "hookIds": [
      "constructor"
    ]
  }
}
~~~

After fix on this branch, the same real selector calls use only own install records:
~~~text
{
  "plugin": {
    "pluginIds": [
      "tracked-constructor"
    ],
    "specOverrides": {
      "tracked-constructor": "constructor"
    }
  },
  "hook": {
    "hookIds": []
  }
}
~~~

## Verification
- node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/cli/plugins-update-selection.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose - passed, 1 file / 8 tests.
- ./node_modules/.bin/oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.core.json src/cli/plugins-update-selection.ts src/cli/plugins-update-selection.test.ts - passed.
- git diff --check - passed.
- Collision check: open PR changed-file search found no open PR modifying src/cli/plugins-update-selection.ts or src/cli/plugins-update-selection.test.ts before opening.

